    "title": "Dad wanted for kidnapping after SWAT responds to DeKalb apartment - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Alex Jones ,\n1 hours ago Dozens of DeKalb County police officers were at an apartment complex on Wednesday night.\nSWAT officers responded to a complex on Woodberry Place to arrest a man with several active warrants.\n[DOWNLOAD: Free WSB-TV News app for alerts as news breaks ]\nInvestigators say Jakarii Eason and his children’s mother got into a dispute at the apartment before she left him there with their two small children.\nChannel 2 Action News was on the scene as SWAT officer investigated.\nOfficers determined that Eason and the children were not inside the apartment.\nTRENDING STORIES:\nThey say they do not believe the children are in danger.\nEason is not in custody. Once arrested, he will be charged with kidnapping, false imprisonment, family violence battery and other charges.\n[SIGN UP: WSB-TV Daily Headlines Newsletter ]",
